Feature: Create a new version of a vocabulary through the API # features/create_version.feature:1
  POST /vocabularies/{vocabularyName}/versions assigns the next number (D7), makes the new
  version ACTIVE and every older ACTIVE version DEPRECATED in one transaction (D4).
  Feature: Create a new version of a vocabulary through the API  # features/create_version.feature:1

  @AC_SIMPL-18173_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18187_AC2 @AC_SIMPL-18190_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18191_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18186_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18194_AC2 @D4 @D6 @D7 @D10 @D26 @D27
  Scenario: A new version gets the next number, is ACTIVE and deprecates the previous one  # features/create_version.feature:9
    Given I am authenticated as "ga-admin"                                                 # features/steps/vm_steps.py:33
    Given a vocabulary "Health" exists                                                     # features/steps/vm_steps.py:51
    When I create a new version of "Health" with:                                          # features/steps/vm_steps.py:137
      | field       | value                                       |
      | description | Healthcare types with extended diagnostics. |
      | changelog   | Added new concept scheme for diagnostics.   |
    Then the response status is 201                                                        # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the Location header is the href of version 2 of "Health"                           # features/steps/vm_steps.py:568
    And the response is version 2 of "Health" with status "ACTIVE"                         # features/steps/vm_steps.py:536
    And the field "changelog" is "Added new concept scheme for diagnostics."               # features/steps/vm_steps.py:452
    And the field "createdBy" is the email of "ga-admin"                                   # features/steps/vm_steps.py:715
    And the response has no validation warnings                                            # features/steps/vm_steps.py:578
    And the versions of "Health" have the statuses "1=DEPRECATED, 2=ACTIVE"                # features/steps/vm_steps.py:673
    And version 1 of "Health" has a lastUpdateDate equal to the creationDate of version 2  # features/steps/vm_steps.py:682

  @AC_SIMPL-18173_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18191_AC1 @D4 @D7
  Scenario: Every previous version is DEPRECATED after the third version                  # features/create_version.feature:25
    Given I am authenticated as "ga-admin"                                                # features/steps/vm_steps.py:33
    Given a vocabulary "Health" exists with 2 versions                                    # features/steps/vm_steps.py:68
    When I create a new version of "Health"                                               # features/steps/vm_steps.py:953
    Then the response status is 201                                                       # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the field "version" is the number 3                                               # features/steps/vm_steps.py:459
    And the versions of "Health" have the statuses "1=DEPRECATED, 2=DEPRECATED, 3=ACTIVE" # features/steps/vm_steps.py:673

