Feature: Health and behaviour when the store is down # features/health_and_resilience.feature:1
  GET /health needs no token (D17). D44 fixes 503 bodies when the store is unreachable.
  Scenarios tagged @store_down need a separate deployment whose store URL points at a port
  where nothing listens; they are excluded by default (see README).
  @D44 @MACH-08 @BLG-hlth-res @API-36
  Scenario: Health reports UP when the store answers    # features/health_and_resilience.feature:7
    Given I am not authenticated                        # features/steps/vm_steps.py:38
    When I send GET "/health"                           # features/steps/vm_steps.py:958
    Then the response status is 200                     # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the response content type is "application/json" # features/steps/vm_steps.py:297
    And the field "status" is "UP"                      # features/steps/vm_steps.py:452

Feature: List, filter, sort and page vocabularies # features/list_vocabularies.feature:1
  GET /vocabularies returns the vocabularies with values of their latest version (D25).
  Filters: D19 and D20. Paging: D22. Sorting: D23. Unknown parameters: D21.
  The store is shared, so every scenario filters on its own run prefix ${run}.
  Feature: List, filter, sort and page vocabularies  # features/list_vocabularies.feature:1

  @AC_SIMPL-18162_AC1 @D22 @D25 @D27 @BLG-col-paging @API-36
