Feature: Read-only search operations # features/search.feature:1
  POST /vocabularies/searches and POST /external-vocabulary/searches are not paged, take at
  most 100 references and keep a fixed order (D38). Viewers may use them (D16).
  Feature: Read-only search operations  # features/search.feature:1

  @D38 @D5 @D25 @D26 @E2
  Scenario: Latest and versioned references come back in request order     # features/search.feature:10
    Given I am authenticated as "ga-viewer"                                # features/steps/vm_steps.py:33
    Given a vocabulary "Health" exists with 3 versions                     # features/steps/vm_steps.py:68
    And a vocabulary "Legacy" exists                                       # features/steps/vm_steps.py:51
    And version 1 of vocabulary "Legacy" has status "DEPRECATED"           # features/steps/vm_steps.py:91
    When I search vocabularies for:                                        # features/steps/vm_steps.py:205
      | name           | version |
      | ${name:Health} |         |
      | ${name:Legacy} | 1       |
    Then the response status is 200                                        # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the search results are:                                            # features/steps/vm_steps.py:904
      | name           | version | status     | latest |
      | ${name:Health} | 3       | ACTIVE     | true   |
      | ${name:Legacy} | 1       | DEPRECATED | false  |
    And the page fields are page 1, pageSize 100, total 2 and totalPages 1 # features/steps/vm_steps.py:805
    And the page links "self, first, prev, next, last" are absent          # features/steps/vm_steps.py:819

