Feature: Change the status of a vocabulary or of one version # features/status.feature:1
  PATCH /vocabularies/{vocabularyName} sets the vocabulary status only; PATCH
  .../versions/{version} sets that version's status only (D3, D4). Same status gives 409.
  Feature: Change the status of a vocabulary or of one version  # features/status.feature:1

  @AC_SIMPL-18175_AC1 @D3 @D25 @API-36
  Scenario: A vocabulary is deprecated and the updated vocabulary is returned             # features/status.feature:9
    Given I am authenticated as "ga-admin"                                                # features/steps/vm_steps.py:33
    Given a vocabulary "Health" exists with 2 versions                                    # features/steps/vm_steps.py:68
    When I change the status of vocabulary "Health" to "DEPRECATED"                       # features/steps/vm_steps.py:153
    Then the response status is 200                                                       # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the response content type is "application/json"                                   # features/steps/vm_steps.py:297
    And the response is vocabulary "Health" with latest version 2 and status "DEPRECATED" # features/steps/vm_steps.py:541
    And the vocabulary "Health" has status "DEPRECATED"                                   # features/steps/vm_steps.py:643
    And the versions of "Health" have the statuses "1=DEPRECATED, 2=ACTIVE"               # features/steps/vm_steps.py:673

  @AC_SIMPL-18175_AC1 @AC_SIMPL-18170_AC2 @D3
