Feature: Role-based access in the UI # features/ui_access.feature:1
  Restricted actions are hidden for users without GA_VOCABULARY_ADMIN (D18).Feature: Accessibility of the main UI pages # features/ui_accessibility.feature:1
  One axe-core check (WCAG 2.1 A and AA rules) per main page. Violations are listed in
  the failure message and in reports/a11y-<page>.json.Feature: Create a vocabulary and a new version in the UI # features/ui_create.feature:1
  Forms: D13, D14, D32, D33, D37, D46. Server rules are the same as the API.Feature: Vocabulary details and version history in the UI # features/ui_details.feature:1
  One screen holds the header and the version history (D35). Warnings: D36.Feature: Vocabulary list in the UI # features/ui_list.feature:1
  Gherkin only; step 60 adds the browser steps. Data is created through the API.
  Screens and texts: D31, D34, D36. Sorting: D23. Filters: D19.Feature: Change the vocabulary status in the UI # features/ui_status.feature:1
  The status-change action offers only the other status (D4). Errors: D24.Feature: Validation feedback in the UI # features/ui_validation.feature:1
  The browser checks syntax on file choice (D13); the server runs syntax and semantic
  validation on submit (D9). Report and warnings panels: D14.Feature: Validation of vocabulary content on creation and new version # features/validation.feature:1
  Two steps run on every POST /vocabularies and POST .../versions: syntax, then semantic (D9).
  Errors block with a 400 validation report; warnings never block and come back in
  validationWarnings of the 201 response (D10, D14).
  Feature: Validation of vocabulary content on creation and new version  # features/validation.feature:1

