Feature: Read a vocabulary, its version history, one version and its content # features/vocabulary_details.feature:1
  GET /vocabularies/{vocabularyName}, .../versions, .../versions/{version} and the
  content downloads (D5, D25, D26, D29). Version list order: D23.
  Feature: Read a vocabulary, its version history, one version and its content  # features/vocabulary_details.feature:1

  @D5 @D25
  Scenario: The vocabulary object shows the latest version                            # features/vocabulary_details.feature:9
    Given I am authenticated as "ga-admin"                                            # features/steps/vm_steps.py:33
    Given a vocabulary "Health" exists with 3 versions                                # features/steps/vm_steps.py:68
    When I send GET "/vocabularies/${name:Health}"                                    # features/steps/vm_steps.py:958
    Then the response status is 200                                                   # features/steps/vm_steps.py:274
    And the response is vocabulary "Health" with latest version 3 and status "ACTIVE" # features/steps/vm_steps.py:541
    And the vocabulary "Health" was created by "ga-admin"                             # features/steps/vm_steps.py:707

  @D24 @negative
